<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vryburg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vryburg is a town in North West Province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>. It was founded in 1882 as the capital of the Republic of Stellaland, its name meaning 'free town', and became the seat of British Bechuanaland in 1885 before passing to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a> in 1895. It is now a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> ranching.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vryburg.jpg" alt="Vryburg" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Leviel · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vryburg_town_hall.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
